# Voice AI Patient Registration Agent

## 1. What we are building
A voice AI agent on a real, dialable U.S. phone number that registers new patients through natural conversation.
The caller dials in, the agent greets them, collects standard U.S. patient demographics, reads everything back,
saves the record to a persistent database only after the caller confirms, tells them they're all set, and ends the call.
A REST API exposes the stored records. If we register "Jane Doe" on call 1, she must exist on call 2.

Context: this is a 3-hour take-home for a Voice AI / Conversational AI Engineer role. Reviewers will phone the number
and hit the API. The brief is explicit: a simple system that works flawlessly beats an ambitious one that crashes
on the first call. When in doubt, pick the simpler option that is guaranteed to work end to end.

## 2. High-level architecture

```
Caller (phone)
   |  PSTN
   v
Vapi  (telephony + speech-to-text + text-to-speech + turn-taking / barge-in)
   |                                              |
   | OpenAI-format /chat/completions (SSE)        | webhooks: tool-calls, end-of-call-report
   v                                              v
FastAPI on Railway
   |-- POST /llm/chat/completions  -> Gemini key pool (rotation + failover) -> Gemini API
   |-- POST /vapi/webhook          -> tool dispatcher -> service layer
   |-- /patients (REST API)        -> service layer
   |-- GET /dashboard              -> simple HTML page that reads /patients
                                          |
                                          v
                          Supabase Postgres (patients, appointments, call_logs)
```

Key rule: the voice agent tools and the REST API call the SAME service layer (`app/services/`).
Validation lives in one place and is enforced server-side no matter what the LLM does.

## 3. Call flow (happy path)
1. Greeting: short, warm, says it's the clinic's AI assistant and what it will do.
2. Collect required fields conversationally. Caller may give several at once or out of order.
3. Once the phone number is known, call `lookup_patient_by_phone`. If a match exists, offer to update instead (bonus).
4. Offer optional fields once: email, insurance, emergency contact, preferred language.
5. Read back every collected field. Ask the caller to confirm or correct.
6. Only after an explicit "yes": call `register_patient` (or `update_patient`).
7. Relay the result. Success: "You're all set, {first_name}." Failure: field-specific re-prompt or graceful apology. Never silence.
8. Bonus: offer a first appointment from mock slots.
9. End the call with Vapi's end-call tool.
10. Vapi sends an end-of-call report. We store transcript + summary in `call_logs`, linked to the patient.

## 4. Functional requirements

### FR-1 Telephony and voice agent
| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-1.1 | Real, dialable U.S. phone number (Vapi free number). |
| FR-1.2 | Natural conversation, not an IVR menu. Should feel like a human intake coordinator. |
| FR-1.3 | LLM-powered (Gemini). Understands varied phrasing, asks clarifying questions, handles corrections. |
| FR-1.4 | Before saving, reads back ALL collected info and asks the caller to confirm or correct any field. |
| FR-1.5 | Invalid data (3-digit phone, future DOB, bad ZIP, unknown state, bad email) triggers a re-prompt for THAT field only. |
| FR-1.6 | After success, brief confirmation ("You're all set, [First Name].") then ends the call gracefully. |

### FR-2 Patient data model
| Field | Type | Validation | Required |
|---|---|---|---|
| patient_id | UUID | Auto-generated | Auto |
| first_name | String | 1-50 chars, letters + hyphens/apostrophes (we also allow single internal spaces, documented) | Yes |
| last_name | String | 1-50 chars, letters + hyphens/apostrophes (same note) | Yes |
| date_of_birth | Date | Valid date, not in the future, MM/DD/YYYY at the API edge | Yes |
| sex | Enum | Male, Female, Other, Decline to Answer | Yes |
| phone_number | String | Valid U.S. 10-digit number, stored as 10 digits | Yes |
| email | String | Valid email format | No |
| address_line_1 | String | Street address | Yes |
| address_line_2 | String | Apt/Suite/Unit | No |
| city | String | 1-100 chars | Yes |
| state | String | Valid 2-letter U.S. state/territory code | Yes |
| zip_code | String | 5-digit or ZIP+4 | Yes |
| insurance_provider | String | Insurance company name | No |
| insurance_member_id | String | Alphanumeric | No |
| preferred_language | String | Default "English" | No |
| emergency_contact_name | String | Full name | No |
| emergency_contact_phone | String | Valid U.S. 10-digit number | No |
| created_at | Timestamp | Auto, UTC | Auto |
| updated_at | Timestamp | Auto on modification, UTC | Auto |
| deleted_at | Timestamp | Null unless soft-deleted | Auto |

Conversation rule: collect required fields first, then make ONE offer, e.g.
"I can also collect your email, insurance information, emergency contact, and preferred language. Would you like to provide any of those?"
The caller opts in. Never force optional fields.

### FR-3 Persistent database
- Supabase Postgres. Data survives server restarts and redeploys (DB lives outside the app container).
- Schema enforces the data model with real column types, NOT NULL, CHECK constraints and an enum for sex.
- Seed 1-2 demo patients with obviously fake data.

### FR-4 REST API
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| GET | /patients | List patients. Optional filters: `?last_name=`, `?date_of_birth=`, `?phone_number=` |
| GET | /patients/{id} | Get one patient by UUID |
| POST | /patients | Create patient. Returns created record incl. patient_id (201) |
| PUT | /patients/{id} | Update patient. Partial updates allowed |
| DELETE | /patients/{id} | Soft delete: set deleted_at. Never hard delete |

API standards:
- Status codes: 200, 201, 400, 404, 422, 500.
- Validate every input server-side. Never trust the voice agent.
- Every response uses the envelope `{ "data": ..., "error": null }` (or `{ "data": null, "error": {...} }`).

### FR-5 Voice agent <-> database integration
- On caller confirmation, the agent triggers a write through the service layer (tool -> service -> DB).
- The agent relays the outcome: success confirmation, or a graceful error message if the write fails.
- Bonus: phone matches an existing patient -> "It looks like we already have a record for [First] [Last]. Would you like to update your information instead?"

## 5. Non-functional requirements
| ID | Area | Expectation |
|---|---|---|
| NFR-1 | Deployment | Running and callable at review time. FastAPI on Railway, DB on Supabase, number on Vapi. |
| NFR-2 | Code quality | Clean, readable, intentional structure. Clear layers: telephony adapter, LLM, service, data, API. |
| NFR-3 | README | Setup, architecture, stack justification, env vars, known limitations/trade-offs, Next Steps, phone number, API base URL, how to test. |
| NFR-4 | Security | No hardcoded keys. Env vars only. `.env` gitignored, `.env.example` committed. Server-side input sanitization. Verify Vapi requests with a shared secret. RLS enabled on Supabase tables. |
| NFR-5 | Observability | Structured JSON logs to stdout. At minimum, log the final collected payload of every call. Also log tool calls, LLM latency, key rotation events, errors. |
| NFR-6 | Latency (our own bar) | Voice UX dies with lag. Target LLM time-to-first-token under ~1s. Stream responses, disable model "thinking", keep replies short, deploy everything in US East. |
| NFR-7 | Resilience (our own bar) | Timeouts on every external call, Gemini key rotation with failover, spoken fallback instead of dead air, DB errors surfaced to the caller. |

## 6. Out of scope
HIPAA compliance, real patient data, dashboard login, outbound calling, ZIP-to-city verification.

## 7. Definition of done
- [ ] Call the number, complete a registration end to end, hear "You're all set".
- [ ] Record visible via GET /patients and on /dashboard.
- [ ] Second call with the same phone number is recognized, and data from call 1 still exists.
- [ ] Every endpoint returns the `{ data, error }` envelope with correct status codes.
- [ ] Invalid DOB / phone / ZIP / state are re-prompted by field during the call and rejected with 422 by the API.
- [ ] README complete, including phone number, API base URL, limitations and Next Steps.
- [ ] No secrets in the repo or in logs.
